    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Description\n\nIf the user defined diagnostic signs are available via `vim.fn.sign.setdefined` or `vim.diagnostic.config`, then use it show diagnostic count in the diagnostic statusline provider.\r\n\r\nI think this would fit into mini.statusline nicely without adding too much extra complexity.\r\n\r\nI'm planning to create a pr with this change if you agree.",
